<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss sight deposits rise to 3,206.1 million Sfr.</title>
<headline>Swiss sight deposits rise to 3,206.1 million Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said sight deposits rose by 187.8 million Swiss francs to 3,206.1 million in the reporting period ended September 10.  </p>
<p>Statement of September 10 in millions of Swiss francs:</p>
<p>					 Latest   Change since August 30</p>
<p> Sight deposits		   3,206.1	plus     187.8</p>
<p> Currency reserves	     39,369.5	plus     749.6</p>
<p> Domestic securities	    3,058.4	plus	10.8</p>
<p> Notes in circulation	  27,739.3	minus    497.1</p>
<p> Other call deposits		479.4	minus     99.6</p>
<p> Government time deposits     2,875.0	plus   1,200.0</p>
<p>Borrowing at the emergency Lombard window rose by 76.1 million francs to 83.0 million in the reporting period. Outstanding borrowing via the discount facility and swaps of money market certificates rose by 139.5 million francs to 1,421.4 million.</p>
<p>An SNB spokesman said the relatively high levels of sight deposits for early September indicated the national bank's continued flexible stance on the money market.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
